	(text "Haptic driver: VBAT -> motor -> PN2222A -> GND.\nD12 high = buzz."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 210.82 43.18 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "18a7d25e-cc10-474d-96e2-7f4ee7f384ef")
	)
	(text "Wiring notes\nAll logic is 3.3 V. Never put 5 V on a GPIO.\nIMU INT1 -> D5 (RTC GPIO) wakes the ESP32 from deep sleep.\nPower the IMU from the 3V pin in the final build: the Feather\n  cuts STEMMA QT power in deep sleep. A QT cable is fine for week-1 tests.\nI2C pull-ups are already on the Adafruit breakouts.\nPN2222A TO-92: flat side facing you, pins left to right = E B C.\nMotor flyback diode: banded end (cathode) to VBAT.\nPin choices are suggestions - any free GPIO 0-21 works."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 129.54 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "53c9f5be-94aa-4bfa-9487-642b9dac1417")
	)
	(text "IR LED drive levels (Vf ~1.3 V, 3.3 V supply):\n  LO  220 ohm  ~8 mA\n  MID 100 ohm ~18 mA\n  HI  33 ohm  ~55 mA (3x 100 ohm in parallel)\nTurn on one channel at a time; send short coded bursts\n(38 kHz carrier via RMT), never a continuous carrier."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 101.6 111.76 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5bba7f38-e31f-4b53-9762-f72afb00fef5")
	)
	(text "MAGNET (not wired): 12 mm N52 disc (stack 2-3) glued to the case,\naxis pointing toward the other ankle.\nThe LIS3MDL on this node is saturated by its own\nmagnet - read magnetic field on Node B only."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 195.58 111.76 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f4d6a882-2924-4788-b073-a12a2287fe80")
	)
